---
// Standalone top-level page — not part of the Starlight docs collection.
// Shares the marketing site's dark visual language (oklch colors, Marcellus +
// IBM Plex Sans/Mono, teal/gold accents) but is deliberately calm: prose and
// tables, no scroll-reveal or canvas work. See AGENTS.md §12 — none of the
// numbers on this page are invented; they trace to spec/decisions/056 and
// spec/behaviors/33-audit-pipeline.md.
const title = "Compliance — Qadi";
const description =
  "What Qadi's audit package assembles, what you still have to bring, and what it explicitly is not.";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Marcellus&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: oklch(0.17 0.014 260);
        --bg-raised: oklch(0.21 0.016 260);
        --bg-card: oklch(0.195 0.015 260);
        --border: oklch(0.32 0.02 260);
        --border-soft: oklch(0.27 0.018 260);
        --text: oklch(0.93 0.006 260);
        --text-muted: oklch(0.72 0.012 260);
        --text-faint: oklch(0.56 0.012 260);
        --teal: oklch(0.72 0.15 195);
        --teal-dim: oklch(0.72 0.15 195 / 0.35);
        --gold: oklch(0.75 0.13 80);
        --gold-dim: oklch(0.75 0.13 80 / 0.35);
        --danger: oklch(0.68 0.17 25);
        --font-serif: "Marcellus", "Iowan Old Style", Georgia, serif;
        --font-sans: "IBM Plex Sans", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        --font-mono: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      html {
        color-scheme: dark;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
        font-size: 16px;
        line-height: 1.65;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--teal);
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      code,
      .mono {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.9em;
      }

      code {
        background: var(--bg-raised);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        border-radius: 4px;
        padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
        color: var(--gold);
      }

      /* ---------- nav ---------- */

      .nav {
        position: sticky;
        top: 0;
        z-index: 20;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        padding: 1rem clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        background: oklch(0.17 0.014 260 / 0.86);
        backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
      }

      .nav-brand {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.6rem;
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .nav-brand:hover {
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .nav-mark {
        width: 1.6rem;
        height: 1.6rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--teal), var(--gold));
        display: inline-block;
        flex-shrink: 0;
      }

      .nav-links {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
      }

      .nav-links a {
        color: var(--text-muted);
      }

      .nav-links a:hover {
        color: var(--teal);
      }

      .nav-links .current {
        color: var(--text);
      }

      /* ---------- layout ---------- */

      main {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem) 6rem;
      }

      section {
        margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
      }

      section:first-of-type {
        margin-top: 0;
      }

      h1 {
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 2.9rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.7rem);
        color: var(--text);
        margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        gap: 0.6rem;
      }

      .section-number {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--teal);
      }

      .section-lede {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.98rem;
        margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
        max-width: 60ch;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--gold);
        margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
      }

      p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
      }

      p.lead {
        font-size: 1.08rem;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      strong {
        color: var(--text);
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      /* ---------- principle callout ---------- */

      .principle {
        margin-top: 2.2rem;
        padding: 1.15rem 1.4rem;
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .principle .mono {
        display: block;
        margin-top: 0.35rem;
        color: var(--text-faint);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
      }

      /* ---------- capability cards ---------- */

      .cap-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      .cap {
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
      }

      .cap h3 {
        margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--text);
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.5rem;
      }

      .cap h3 code {
        font-size: 0.82em;
      }

      .cap p {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.94rem;
      }

      .tag {
        display: inline-block;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.68rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--teal);
        border: 1px solid var(--teal-dim);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
      }

      /* ---------- you-bring list ---------- */

      .bring-list {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.9rem;
      }

      .bring-list li {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.85rem;
        padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-size: 0.94rem;
      }

      .bring-list .glyph {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        color: var(--gold);
        flex-shrink: 0;
      }

      .bring-list p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      /* ---------- not-list ---------- */

      .not-list {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
        padding: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.7rem;
      }

      .not-list li {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.7rem;
        font-size: 0.96rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        line-height: 1.55;
      }

      .not-list .glyph {
        color: var(--danger);
        flex-shrink: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
      }

      .callout-warn {
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid oklch(0.68 0.17 25 / 0.4);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--danger);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 1.15rem 1.4rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .callout-warn p:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }

      /* ---------- evidence table ---------- */

      .evidence-stats {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
      }

      .stat {
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
      }

      .stat .num {
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-size: 1.9rem;
        color: var(--teal);
        line-height: 1;
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
      }

      .stat .label {
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        color: var(--text-faint);
      }

      .inv-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        display: block;
      }

      .inv-table tbody {
        display: table;
        width: 100%;
      }

      .inv-table th,
      .inv-table td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        vertical-align: top;
      }

      .inv-table th {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--text-faint);
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      .inv-table td.id {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        color: var(--gold);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .inv-table td {
        color: var(--text-muted);
      }

      .measured-line {
        margin-top: 1.4rem;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        color: var(--text-faint);
      }

      .measured-line strong {
        color: var(--teal);
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
      }

      /* ---------- footer / doc links ---------- */

      .doc-links {
        margin-top: 4rem;
        padding-top: 2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
      }

      .doc-links p {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 0.94rem;
      }

      .doc-links ul {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.55rem;
      }

      .doc-links a {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      footer.site-footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
        padding: 2rem clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        text-align: center;
        color: var(--text-faint);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }

      @media (max-width: 620px) {
        .evidence-stats {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .nav-links {
          gap: 0.9rem;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="nav">
      <a class="nav-brand" href="/">
        <span class="nav-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        qadi
      </a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
        <a class="current" href="/compliance/" aria-current="page">Compliance</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/leaderiop/qadi" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust &amp; assurance</p>
        <h1>Compliance</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          This page describes, plainly, what Qadi's audit package assembles for you, what you
          still have to bring yourself, and what it explicitly does not do. No compliance
          certification of any kind is being claimed anywhere on this page — what follows is a
          factual account of wiring and test coverage, not a regulatory attestation.
        </p>
        <div class="principle">
          Every capability described below is wired into the real evaluation path and covered by
          the tests cited beside it — nothing on this page is exported but unused.
          <span class="mono">This is a design principle Qadi's audit package is built to, not a marketing claim.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2><span class="section-number">01</span> What Qadi assembles</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          <code>@qadi/audit</code> composes five capabilities into one pipeline, hung off the
          same decision sink every evaluation already writes through.
        </p>
        <div class="cap-list">
          <div class="cap">
            <h3><code>AuditDecisionSinkLive</code> <span class="tag">wired</span></h3>
            <p>
              An audit trail write, best-effort staging, and an internal circuit breaker,
              composed into one assembled pipeline reachable through a single call. You are not
              handed three individually-correct pieces to wire together yourself — encoding,
              staging (if configured), and the trail write all happen inside the one
              <code>record()</code> call every evaluation already makes. While the breaker is
              open, a wired staging store still receives the entry even though the trail write is
              skipped, so nothing is silently lost if a staging backend is configured.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap">
            <h3>Retention, archival &amp; decommissioning <span class="tag">pure functions</span></h3>
            <p>
              Retention selection, chain-integrity checking across sequence numbers, archival, and
              a six-step decommissioning checklist all ship as plain, invocable functions and
              data. They run when you call them — nothing here is triggered on a timer or a
              schedule internal to the library.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap">
            <h3>E-signature capture <span class="tag">wired</span></h3>
            <p>
              A <code>hasSignature</code> policy check, an obligation handler, and a
              <code>SignatureCapturePort</code> you implement, wired together through the same
              obligation mechanism the rest of policy enforcement already uses. Capturing a
              signature is a condition of enforcement, not a side channel bolted on afterward.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2><span class="section-number">02</span> What you still bring</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Every capability above needs real storage, identity, or crypto behind it. Qadi supplies
          none of that itself — it defines the ports and wires the calls that use them.
        </p>
        <ul class="bring-list">
          <li>
            <span class="glyph">01</span>
            <p>
              <strong>A storage backend for the audit trail port.</strong> Qadi does not open a
              database connection, generate a key, or assume a schema — you implement where
              entries are durably written.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="glyph">02</span>
            <p>
              <strong>Crypto and identity for signature capture.</strong> The signature capture
              port is a plain interface; what actually authenticates a signer and produces a
              signature record is entirely your implementation.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="glyph">03</span>
            <p>
              <strong>Your own retention schedule.</strong> Qadi never runs a retention job on a
              timer of its own — you invoke retention, archival, and decommissioning yourself, on
              whatever cadence your policies require.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="glyph">04</span>
            <p>
              <strong>Your own IQ/OQ/PQ evidence.</strong> Installation, operational, and
              performance qualification for your deployment are your organization's
              responsibility to produce and hold — Qadi's tests establish that its own pipeline
              behaves as documented, not that your particular deployment meets a regulatory
              standard.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2><span class="section-number">03</span> What this explicitly is not</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Stated plainly rather than left implicit, because the gap between "wired and tested"
          and "compliant" is exactly the gap this page exists to be honest about.
        </p>
        <ul class="not-list">
          <li><span class="glyph">—</span> Not a certification of any kind, from any body.</li>
          <li><span class="glyph">—</span> Not 21 CFR Part 11 support out of the box.</li>
          <li>
            <span class="glyph">—</span> Not a claim that your deployment is audit-ready simply
            because this package is installed.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout-warn">
          <p>
            <strong><code>hasSignature</code> is trust-on-presence.</strong> It checks whether a
            caller-supplied signature record exists with a matching meaning and, optionally,
            signer role — the same record your own signature capture port produced earlier. It
            does not perform a live cryptographic check of any kind, and it models no
            reauthentication step.
          </p>
          <p>
            No default signature capture implementation ships — not even a no-op one. A shipped
            no-op would let a signature obligation silently appear satisfied with nothing behind
            it, which is exactly the false-compliance affordance this design deliberately avoided.
            Without your own port wired, enforcement fails closed instead.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2><span class="section-number">04</span> Evidence</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Measured, not asserted. These are concrete numbers from the test suite, not descriptive
          claims about intent.
        </p>
        <div class="evidence-stats">
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="num">92%</span>
            <span class="label">Mutation score on <code>packages/audit</code> — <code>pnpm check</code> gate 20</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="num">5</span>
            <span class="label">Formally stated invariants, INV-QD-051 through INV-QD-055</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <table class="inv-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Invariant</th>
              <th>What it covers</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="id">INV-QD-051</td>
              <td>Staging presence or absence never changes the committed audit entries.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="id">INV-QD-052</td>
              <td>Once a circuit breaker trips, a write is never attempted again until reset.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="id">INV-QD-053</td>
              <td>Retained and purged entries partition the full set — no overlap, no gap.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="id">INV-QD-054</td>
              <td>Chain-integrity checking detects every gap and duplicate sequence number.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="id">INV-QD-055</td>
              <td>
                The signature obligation handler calls capture exactly once, and the obligation
                record matches its outcome.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="measured-line">
          <strong>92%</strong> mutation score · <strong>5</strong> invariants · <strong>1</strong> assembled pipeline
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="doc-links">
        <p>For the API reference, see the <code>@qadi/audit</code> package documentation:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/packages/audit/">/docs/packages/audit/</a> — overview</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/packages/audit/capabilities/">/docs/packages/audit/capabilities/</a> — the assembled pipeline, retention, and archival</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/packages/audit/signatures/">/docs/packages/audit/signatures/</a> — e-signature capture</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>Qadi is an Effect-native authorization library for TypeScript.</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
